1-opt-9ed9a234-706d-46bb-bf46-9e9b391b2cb3.jpg?aio=w-300;h-300;fill;)\n![San Petros Residency](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/san-petros-residency-project-location-image1-5488-opt-29656950-639c-4d61-ae57-a6d074811027.jpg?aio=w-300;h-300;fill;)\n![San Petros Residency](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/san-petros-residency-project-floor-plans1-8779-opt-7ff39c24-52dc-4662-9976-01cd0aae0019.jpg?aio=w-300;h-300;fill;)\n![San Petros Properties Developer Logo]( \"San Petros Properties\")\n\n## [San Petros Residency in Dadar West, Mumbai](https://www.squareyards.com/san-petros-residency-dadar-west-mumbai-npd-345559 \"San Petros Residency\")\n\nPrice On Request\n\nPrice On Request\n\n![Loading more projects](/assets/images/infinite-loader.gif)\n\n### \n\n## 97+ New Projects in Mumbai South, Mumbai\n\n### Mumbai South Launch Market at a Glance\n\n## What Are New Launch Projects in South Mumbai?\n\nA new launch project in South Mumbai is a residential development that opens for booking while still under construction, with possession set for a future date. You select a unit from the full available spread and settle payment in instalments as the build advances. The 97+ new construction projects in South Mumbai on this page sit within 96 total listings across the belt, covering apartments, villas, penthouses, plots and studios.\n\n## Why Is South Mumbai India's Most Closely Watched Luxury Market?\n\nSouth Mumbai covers the island city's oldest and most prestigious addresses, from Malabar Hill and Cuffe Parade to Worli, Lower Parel and Parel. What sets new residential projects in South Mumbai apart from anywhere else in the country is a simple structural fact: there is almost no fresh land left. Nearly every new building project in South Mumbai today is a redevelopment, replacing an older structure with a modern tower on the same footprint, which keeps genuinely new supply permanently scarce against demand from legacy wealth, family offices and NRI buyers.\n\nWorli has emerged as the corridor where this redevelopment wave is most visible, with contemporary high-rises replacing older mill-era buildings and setting new benchmarks for ultra-luxury transactions in India. Malabar Hill, Cuffe Parade and Altamount Road remain the old-money core, where new construction in South Mumbai is rare enough that each fresh launch becomes a market event in its own right. Lower Parel and Parel, built largely on former textile-mill land, offer the most accessible entry into a South Mumbai address for buyers who want newer inventory and modern amenities. Developers including Lodha, Kalpataru, Runwal, Rustomjee, The Wadhwa Group, Ruparel, Godrej, Chandak, Ajmera, Mahindra Lifespaces are active across this landscape, and MahaRERA registration is mandatory for every project.\n\n## Which Part of South Mumbai Fits Your Budget?\n\n## What Is Driving New Construction in South Mumbai?\n\n## New Launch Property Types in South Mumbai\n\nApartments dominate the pipeline across South Mumbai, with penthouses, villas, studios and plots making up a smaller but significant share, concentrated in the redevelopment-heavy corridors.\n\n| **Format** | **What it offers** | **Best for** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Apartments** | **High-rise redevelopment towers with sea or city views** | **Legacy buyers, professionals and NRI investors** |\n| **[Penthouses](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/penthouses-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Top-floor residences with expansive layouts** | **UHNIs and family offices seeking a signature address** |\n| **[Villas](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/villas-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Independent bungalow-style residences, where still available** | **Buyers wanting rare standalone privacy in the island city** |\n| **[Studios](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/studio-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Compact units in select redevelopment towers** | **Rental investors and single professionals** |\n| **[Plots](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/plots-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **MahaRERA-registered redevelopment land parcels** | **Long-horizon investors and boutique developers** |\n\n### Picking the right size\n\nNew residential projects in South Mumbai run from 2 BHK through 5 BHK and penthouse formats, with 3 and 4 BHK the most active configurations across the belt. Who each tends to suit:\n\n| **Configuration** | **Typically Suits** |\n| --- | --- |\n| **[1 BHK](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/1-bhk-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Compact entry-level units for professionals and rental investors** |\n| **[2 BHK](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/2-bhk-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Professionals and smaller households wanting a South Mumbai address** |\n| **[3 BHK](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/3-bhk-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Families and NRI buyers, the most active configuration in the belt** |\n| **[4 BHK](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/4-bhk-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Larger households and premium buyers in Worli and Lower Parel towers** |\n| **[5 BHK](https://www.squareyards.com/sale/5-bhk-for-sale-in-mumbai-south-mumbai)** | **Large-format homes for premium and multi-generational buyers** |\n\n## Reading New Launch Prices in South Mumbai\n\n### What is the average new launch price in South Mumbai?\n\nNew launches across South Mumbai average ₹50,600 (psf), against a Mumbai-wide average of ₹31,725 (psf). The range within the belt is exceptionally wide: Malabar Hill and Altamount Road sit at the very top, Worli and Cuffe Parade follow closely behind, and Lower Parel, Parel and Byculla offer the most accessible entry into a South Mumbai address. Many listings carry Price on Request, reflecting the bespoke, negotiation-driven nature of ultra-luxury transactions in this belt.\n\n### How do I compare prices within South Mumbai?\n\nFilter to a single locality before comparing on price, since Malabar Hill and Lower Parel operate on entirely different pricing logic within the same broader belt. Comparing Least Price and Highest Price within one locality and configuration gives the clearest read on where a launch sits.\n\n## Developers and Projects in South Mumbai\n\n### Who is building new residential projects in South Mumbai?\n\nActive developers across South Mumbai include Lodha, Kalpataru, Runwal, Rustomjee, The Wadhwa Group, Ruparel, Godrej, Chandak, Ajmera, Mahindra Lifespaces. All new projects must carry MahaRERA registration, which buyers can check on the Maharashtra RERA portal before a site visit. Given the redevelopment-heavy nature of this market, also verify the developer's approvals discipline and track record in dense urban redevelopment specifically.\n\n### What is happening across Mumbai right now?\n\nNew properties in South Mumbai extend well beyond the current new launch pipeline; buyers exploring new projects in South Mumbai more broadly can also look at ready and under-construction stock. Beyond South Mumbai, new launches drawing attention across Mumbai include Kalpataru Vian, Mahindra Rainforest, LnT Ahana, Purva Estrella, Mahindra Marina 64, averaging ₹31,725 (psf). Established Mumbai developments across all stages include Arihant Aspire, LnT Crestoria Estate, Hiranandani Fortune City, Godrej Green Terraces, Godrej Nexspace. Cross-check any project on MahaRERA before proceeding.\n\n## Shortlisting New Launches in South Mumbai\n\n## More South Mumbai and Mumbai Pages\n\nThese pages cover other parts of the South Mumbai and Mumbai market.\n\n| **Looking for** | **Go to** |\n| --- | --- |\n| **All projects** | [Projects in South Mumbai](https://www.squareyards.com/projects-in-mumbai-south-mumbai) |\n| **Ready now** | [Ready to move projects in South Mumbai](https://www.squareyards.com/ready-to-move-projects-in-mumbai-south-mumbai) |\n| **Still building** | [Under construction projects in South Mumbai](https://www.squareyards.com/under-construction-projects-in-mumbai-south-mumbai) |\n| **All Mumbai new** | [New projects in Mumbai](https://www.squareyards.com/new-projects-in-mumbai) |\n\n## Stamp Duty and Registration Charges in South Mumbai\n\nAdd these government charges on top of the quoted price. Mumbai follows Maharashtra's stamp duty structure, with rates that vary by ownership type.\n\n| **Charge** | **Rate** |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Stamp Duty (Male ownership)** | **6%** |\n| **Stamp Duty (Female ownership)** | **5%** |\n| **Stamp Duty (Joint ownership)** | **5.5%** |\n| **Registration Charges** | **1% of the total value** |\n\n## New Launch FAQs for South Mumbai\n\n### Q: How many new launch projects are there in South Mumbai?\n\nA: South Mumbai currently has 97+ new residential projects open for booking within 96 total listings. Across Mumbai there are 96+ new launches.\n\n### Q: What is the average price for new launches in South Mumbai?\n\nA: New launches in South Mumbai average ₹50,600 (psf), against a Mumbai-wide average of ₹31,725 (psf). Malabar Hill and Altamount Road sit at the top of the range; Lower Parel and Byculla offer the most accessible entry.\n\n### Q: What types of property are available in new residential projects in South Mumbai?\n\nA: Apartments lead the pipeline, with penthouses, villas, studios and plots also available, concentrated in the belt's redevelopment-heavy corridors.\n\n### Q: Which part of South Mumbai has the most new building projects?\n\nA: Worli and Lower Parel currently see the most redevelopment activity and new supply. Malabar Hill and Cuffe Parade see rare, high-value launches given their near-total land scarcity.\n\n### Q: What is driving new construction in South Mumbai?\n\nA: Redevelopment of ageing structures on scarce land, the fully operational Coastal Road between Marine Lines and Worli, Mumbai Metro Line 3, the upcoming Sewri Worli Connector, and sustained legacy wealth and NRI demand are the main drivers.\n\n### Q: Who are the active developers in South Mumbai?\n\nA;They include Lodha, Kalpataru, Runwal, Rustomjee, The Wadhwa Group, Ruparel, Godrej, Chandak, Ajmera, Mahindra Lifespaces. Projects currently drawing enquiries include Godrej Trilogy, JP Codename Matunga Origins, Mahindra BeaconHill, Raymond The Address By GS, Lodha Worli.\n\n### Q: What are the stamp duty and registration charges in Mumbai?\n\nA: Mumbai follows Maharashtra's rates: 6% for male buyers, 5% for female buyers and 5.5% for joint ownership. On top of that, registration takes another 1% of the property's total value.\n\n### Q: What does a new launch mean in South Mumbai?\n\nA: A new launch is a residential development that opens for sale while under construction, with possession set for a future date. You reserve a unit early and pay in stages as the build advances.\n\n### Q: What should I check before booking a new property in South Mumbai?\n\nA: Verify the MahaRERA registration and possession date, confirm whether the project is a redevelopment and review the underlying land title, and check the developer's completion record before making any payment.\n\nPersonalized home recommendations based on your lifestyle, location, and budget.\n\n![Smarter home match recommendation preview](/assets/images/recommandation-images/recommendation-preview.png)\n![Personalized home matching](/assets/images/recommandation-images/icon-star.svg)\n\nRecommendations tailored to your real needs.\n\n![Smarter locality suggestions](/assets/images/recommandation-images/pin-icon.svg)\n\nDiscover neighborhoods that fit your lifestyle.\n\n![Budget aware recommendations](/assets/images/recommandation-images/wallet-icon.svg)\n\nFind homes that match your budget.\n\n![Personalized property recommendation cards](/assets/images/recommandation-images/property-img.png)\n![voice search]()![Bangalore city icon](/assets/images/city-svg-icons/bangalore.svg)\n![Chennai city icon](/assets/images/city-svg-icons/chennai.svg)\n![Delhi city icon](/ass